isabel: Quick heads-up: new edge onboarding sample (edge-quick-client) shows a typing collapse after the edge bundle step. Generic inference for our `client.authRetry()` helper becomes `any` in consumer code only when packaged for the edge. Repro is small.

nate: can you paste the minimal repro and the sample tsconfig? is this the bundler or our published typings?

isabel: minimal below. Works in node dev and node build but after the swc/esbuild edge pipeline the consumer sees `any`.
```ts
// packages/sdk/src/auth.ts
export type Retry<T = unknown> = { attempts?: number; payload?: T }
export function authRetry<T>(cb: () => Promise<void>, opts?: Retry<T>): { do: () => T }
export function authRetry(cb: () => Promise<void>, opts?: Retry<any>) { return { do: () => (opts?.payload as any) } }

// consumer.ts
const c = authRetry(async () => {}, { attempts: 2, payload: { user: 'anna' } })
// expect c.do() => { user: string } but becomes any after edge packaging
```

ravi: that pattern keeps showing up. TL;DR: implementation signature with `any` leaks into the published .d.ts and certain moduleResolution modes (bundler) + dual exports cause TS to resolve the wrong declaration order. Edge bundlers that rewrite imports can make this surface only for edge builds.

jay: short-term mitigation: update the example tsconfig to `moduleResolution: node16` and note it in the README. That makes TS pick the ESM types consistently.

isabel: agreed on short-term. longer-term we should stop publishing impl signatures. Options: 1) emit only `export declare function` overloads in the published d.ts, mark the real impl `/** @internal */` and set `stripInternal: true` on declaration emit; 2) prefer `unknown` over `any` on public generics and provide a small `narrowPayload<T>(p: Retry<T>) => Retry<T>` helper as an opt-in narrowing.

nate: i prefer option 1 for non-breaking safety. Also explicitly set `types` paths in `exports` to avoid resolver ambiguity. We should add a tiny typing smoke test in examples CI that runs `tsc --noEmit` under both `moduleResolution: bundler` and `moduleResolution: node16`.

ci-bot: issue created: DX-5021 - "edge bundle widens generic overload to any in onboarding sample" (assignee: @ravi).

ravi: plan: add a small test in `packages/sdk/typing-tests/edge-auth.ts`, change declaration emit so published d.ts only exposes `declare` overloads, add `types` subpath entries in `exports` field, and update example tsconfig/readme as a temporary mitigation. Will open PR and link DX-5021.

isabel: holding sample merge until the typings PR lands so new users don't hit this. Thanks y'all. :thumbsup:
